msgid "In Tanzania, the Access to Information Act, 2016 lets you ask a public body for records. Name the project and the financial year, and say where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, the Commission for Human Rights and Good Governance is the national oversight office."
msgstr "In Tanzania, the Access to Information Act, 2016 lets you ask a public body for records. Name the project and the financial year, and say where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, the Commission for Human Rights and Good Governance is the national oversight office."

msgid "Burundi does not yet have a standalone access-to-information statute. The Constitution recognizes the right to information. Write to the public body that holds the file. Name the project, the financial year, and where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, the Ombudsman (Médiateur de la République) is a national civic route. This is not legal advice."
msgstr "Burundi does not yet have a standalone access-to-information statute. The Constitution recognizes the right to information. Write to the public body that holds the file. Name the project, the financial year, and where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, the Ombudsman (Médiateur de la République) is a national civic route. This is not legal advice."

msgid "In Nigeria, the Freedom of Information Act, 2011 lets you ask a public institution for records. Put the request in writing, name the project, and say where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, you can apply to a court. The Public Complaints Commission is a further civic route."
msgstr "In Nigeria, the Freedom of Information Act, 2011 lets you ask a public institution for records. Put the request in writing, name the project, and say where to send the reply. If there is no useful answer, you can apply to a court. The Public Complaints Commission is a further civic route."
